%% 05 — Request authorization, multipart upload and binary read
%% Sources: .planning/06-api-contracts.md §1.9, §2.1-2.3, §5.18-5.21, §8.3-8.5; 05-database-design.md §3.5
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant B as Browser
  participant P as Reverse proxy
  participant A as apps/api
  participant D as Cloudflare D1
  participant S as Upload storage

  Note over B,P: Flow A - authorized read of an owned Attachment
  B->>P: GET /api/v1/attachments/:id/content?variant=full with sid cookie
  P->>A: forward on one origin, no authorization decision
  A->>A: read sid, SHA-256 it, check Origin on unsafe methods only
  A->>D: SELECT session JOIN users by token_hash, expires_at, last_used_at
  alt no session, expired or idle-revoked
    A-->>B: 401 UNAUTHENTICATED with expired Set-Cookie
  else session valid
    A->>D: SELECT attachment WHERE id = $1 AND user_id = $sessionUserId
    alt zero rows - absent and foreign are indistinguishable
      A-->>B: 404 NOT_FOUND
    else row owned
      A->>S: open storage_key for variant full or thumb
      A-->>B: 200 bytes with ETag, private max-age 86400, nosniff
      Note over B: ETag match on the next request returns 304
    end
  end

  Note over B,P: Flow B - multipart upload with two-gate validation and thumbnail
  B->>P: POST /api/v1/attachments multipart file, targetType, targetId
  P->>A: forward
  A->>A: exactly one file part, file under 5 MiB, else 413 or 422
  A->>D: SELECT target WHERE id = $targetId AND user_id = $sessionUserId
  alt target absent or foreign
    A-->>B: 404 NOT_FOUND, nothing written
  else target owned
    A->>A: gate 1 sniff magic bytes in image/jpeg, image/png, image/webp, else 415
    A->>A: gate 2 sharp decode metadata, else 422 undecodable_image
    A->>S: write full file via temp then rename
    A->>S: derive thumbnail, longest edge 320 px, WebP
    A->>D: BEGIN, parent row FOR UPDATE, count existing rows
    alt target already holds 10 attachments
      A->>S: unlink full file and thumbnail
      A-->>B: 422 attachment_limit
    else under the cap
      A->>D: INSERT attachments, COMMIT
      A-->>B: 201 Created with AttachmentSummary thumbUrl and fullUrl
    end
  end
  Note over A,S: The row is the commit point - no row ever points at a missing binary
